# Introduce Advanced Flow to `ManageSecurityStructure ` feature 
Which is a **really** is advanced (complex) feature.

#### N.B. when reviewing this, remember, this is a Proof of Concept version of these features. No reference UX exists, no reference UI exists, no copy exists. I've design this from these Figma prototypes, which were much much too simplistic and did not properly capture the complexity of it all. So when reviewing this, save us time by refraining from how Views are implemented, how ViewState is implemented etc. Instead focus on the logic and especially how generics are used in `FactorSourcesOfKindList` feature, which proved tricky. The use case is this: for **simple flow** only certain FactorSource kinds are allowed for certain roles, e.g .`FactorSourcesOfKindList<SecurityQuestionsFactorSource>` for `confirmationRole`, but for **advanced flow** multiple factor source kinds are allowed why we use `FactorSourcesOfKindList<FactorSource>`. I think the current solution is OK, but maybe it can be cleaned up?

Here is the [Figma wireframe](https://www.figma.com/file/KnKaHox4bd4NZvme6nJP1Z/Babylon-Wallet---UX-Wireframes-(P10)?type=design&node-id=2764-14630&mode=design&t=YzWzKZfIi287nwH9-4) I've worked from: 
<img width="1623" alt="Screenshot 2023-06-27 at 15 22 28" src="https://github.com/radixdlt/babylon-wallet-ios/assets/116169792/0f5b029c-0c72-46b3-83a1-ab38548e1759">



Furthermore:
1. Change ProfileSnapshot to let FactorSource's be "flagged for deletion" which hides them in UI
2. Split `SecurityStructureConfiguration` into `SecurityStructureConfigurationReferences` (`FactorSourceID` level, used by Profile Snapshot) and `SecurityStructureConfigurationDetailed` (on `FactorSource` level, never saved in Profile, logic/UI only)
3. Add `Copy JSON` button to Debug Inspect Profile
4. Split `SecurityStructure` file into many files (removed unused `TemplateStructure..`.)


